<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n95170" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκορπί-ος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>scorpion</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				169
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Euthd.</u>
				290a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sammelb.</u>
				1267.7
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A.D.)</span>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. ὁ
			χερσαῖος</span> (v. infr. <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>) <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				555a23
			</span></i>: prov., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ παντὶ λίθῳ σκορπίον φυλάσσεο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Praxill.
					4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν παντὶ ς. φρουρεῖ λίθῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					37
				</span></i>
			; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκορπίον ὀκτώπουν
			ἐγείρεις</span> 'let sleeping dogs lie', <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥσπερ ἔχις ἢ ς. ἠρκὼς τὸ κέντρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					25.52
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> a sea-fish,
			prob. <i>Scorpaena scrofa</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				261.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Diocl.Fr.
				135
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				508b17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.977f
			</span></i>; used (like the <i>mugilis</i> in Catull.<i><span class="en">
				15.19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Juv.
				10.317
			</span></i>) to punish adulterers, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.Com.
				173.21
			</span></i>; dub. sens. in <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>3 Ki.</u>
				12.11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>scorpion furze, Genista acanthoclada</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				6.1.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.4.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>scorpion root, Doronicum caucasicum</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				9.13.6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θηλυφόνον</span>
			, ib.<i><span class="en">
				9.18.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b> the
			constellation <u>Scorpio</u>, <i><span class="en">
				Cleostrat.
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				85
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eudox.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Hipparch.
				1.2.20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eratosth.
				<u>Cat.</u>
				7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>V.</b> an engine of
			war for discharging arrows, <i><span class="en">
				Hero
				<u>Bel.</u>
				74.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Marc.</u>
				15
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκορπίων σωλῆνες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					22.1627.333
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>VI.</b> a stone,
				<i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>L.</u>
				500
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				494
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>